# What NOT to put in the published archive.
#
# HOW PUB DECIDES. It lists the files ON DISK under this directory and leaves
# out every one an ignore rule matches. ⛔ Whether git tracks a file plays no
# part: a committed file an ignore rule matches is left out, and an untracked
# file no rule matches is published.
#
#   * Dot-files and `pubspec.lock` are always left out, by pub's own rules.
#   * ⚠️ In each directory a `.pubignore` REPLACES that directory's
#     `.gitignore` -- it does not add to it. So everything package/.gitignore
#     excluded is re-stated here. For `.dart_tool/` and `pubspec.lock` below
#     that is belt and braces, since pub's own rules already drop both.
#   * ⛔ It does not replace any OTHER directory's `.gitignore`. Inside a git
#     repository pub applies the ignore files of every directory from the
#     repository root down, so the repository-root `.gitignore` still decides
#     for the paths it matches: a native library it matches is absent from
#     the archive whether or not it is committed.
#
# Source: dart-lang/pub at ec276d10 -- the revision Dart 3.13.1's DEPS pins --
# `lib/src/package.dart`, `listFiles` and `_basicIgnoreRules`: "If [dir] is
# inside a git repository, all ignore files from the repo root are considered.
# For each directory a .pubignore takes precedence over a .gitignore." Pub runs
# `git ls-files` only in its gitignore validator, to WARN that a checked-in
# file is ignored and "Previous versions of Pub would include those".
#
# So in the public repository, committing the shipped libraries is not what
# ships them: they ship only if no ignore file between that repository's root
# and the library matches them. Verify with `dart pub publish --dry-run`, which
# lists the archive, never by reading this file.

# The suite and its configuration. Certification runs in the repository, on the
# repository's tests; the archive carries none of them, so shipping them would
# ship an instrument nobody who receives it can run.
test/
dart_test.yaml

# Binding generation is a maintainer activity against the C header and the
# build-generated zenoh-c headers, none of which are in the archive.
ffigen.yaml

# Re-stated from package/.gitignore; pub's own rules drop both anyway (above).
.dart_tool/
pubspec.lock

# Editor / assistant state.
.claude/

# ── Deliberately NOT excluded, and each for a reason ──
#   lib/      the package
#   hook/     the build hook -- without it the consumer gets no native asset
#   native/   the prebuilt libraries; they ARE the distribution mechanism
#   example/  pub.dev renders it, and it is the CLI cookbook
#   skills/   reserved for the consumer skill (roadmap R32); absent today
#   analysis_options.yaml  small, and pana reads the package as configured
